{"extractedPreview":"{\n  \"title\": \"Mystical Forest Path\",\n  \"slug\": \"mystical-forest-path\",\n  \"description\": \"In a mystical forest, there are N trees arranged in a straight line. Each tree has a height represented by a positive integer. A path is considered mystical if the height of each tree in the path is strictly increasing. You are given an array of tree heights and a positive integer K. Your task is to find the length of the longest mystical path that can be formed by removing at most K trees from the forest.\\n...","level":"error","message":"JSON parse failed after extraction in generateProblem","service":"code-execution-backend api","timestamp":"2026-06-01T05:17:04.180Z"}
{"level":"error","message":"AI returned invalid JSON in generateProblem","raw":"{\n  \"title\": \"Mystical Forest Path\",\n  \"slug\": \"mystical-forest-path\",\n  \"description\": \"In a mystical forest, there are N trees arranged in a straight line. Each tree has a height represented by a positive integer. A path is considered mystical if the height of each tree in the path is strictly increasing. You are given an array of tree heights and a positive integer K. Your task is to find the length of the longest mystical path that can be formed by removing at most K trees from the forest.\\n\\nFunction Signature: `function longestMysticalPath(trees: number[], K: number): number`\\n\\nInput:\\n- `trees`: An array of positive integers representing the heights of the trees. (1 <= trees.length <= 1000, 1 <= trees[i] <= 10000)\\n- `K`: A positive integer representing the maximum number of trees that can be removed. (0 <= K <= trees.length)\\n\\nOutput:\\n- A single integer representing the length of the longest mystical path.\\n\\nExamples:\\n1. `longestMysticalPath([5, 3, 6, 7, 4], 2) => \"3\"`\\n2. `longestMysticalPath([1, 2, 3, 4, 5], 0) => \"5\"`\\n3. `longestMysticalPath([10, 9, 8, 7, 6], 3) => \"2\"`\",\n  \"referenceSolution\": \"function longestMysticalPath(trees, K) {\\n    const n = trees.length;\\n    const dp = Array(n).fill(1);\\n    for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) {\\n        for (let j = 0; j < i; j++) {\\n            if (trees[i] > trees[j]) {\\n                dp[i] = Math.max(dp[i], dp[j] + 1);\\n            }\\n        }\\n    }\\n    dp.sort((a, b) => b - a);\\n    return Math.max(0, dp[K] - K);\\n}\",\n  \"testCases\": [\n    {\"input\": \"[5, 3, 6, 7, 4], 2\", \"expected\": \"3\", \"isHidden\": false},\n    {\"input\": \"[1, 2, 3, 4, 5], 0\", \"expected\": \"5\", \"isHidden\": false},\n    {\"input\": \"[10, 9, 8, 7, 6], 3\", \"expected\": \"2\", \"isHidden\": true},\n    {\"input\": \"[4, 2, 3, 6, 10, 1, 12], 3\", \"expected\": \"5\", \"isHidden\": true},\n    {\"input\": \"[5, 1, 3, 2, 4], 1\", \"expected\": \"4\", \"isHidden\": true},\n    {\"input\": \"[1, 3, 2, 4, 6, 5], 2\", \"expected\": \"4\", \"isHidden\": true},\n    {\"input\": \"[9, 8, 7, 6, 5, 4, 3, 2, 1], 4\", \"expected\": \"2\", \"isHidden\": true}\n  ]\n}","service":"code-execution-backend api","timestamp":"2026-06-01T05:17:04.181Z"}
