{"level":"error","message":"AI returned invalid JSON in generateProblem","raw":"{\n  \"title\": \"Optimal Robot Path in a Grid with Obstacles and Teleports\",\n  \"slug\": \"optimal-robot-path-grid-obstacles-teleports\",\n  \"description\": \"A robot is placed in a grid of size N x M. The grid contains obstacles and teleportation points. The robot can move up, down, left, or right, but cannot move through obstacles. Teleportation points instantly move the robot to another specified point in the grid. The goal is to find the minimum number of moves required for the robot to reach the target point from the starting point, considering the obstacles and teleportation points.\n\n  Input:\n  - The first line contains two integers N and M (1 <= N, M <= 100) representing the dimensions of the grid.\n  - The second line contains two integers Sx and Sy (1 <= Sx <= N, 1 <= Sy <= M) representing the starting point of the robot.\n  - The third line contains two integers Tx and Ty (1 <= Tx <= N, 1 <= Ty <= M) representing the target point of the robot.\n  - The next N lines contain M characters each, representing the grid. Each character can be:\n    - '.' representing an empty cell.\n    - '#' representing an obstacle.\n    - 'T' representing a teleportation point. The first 'T' encountered in the grid is the starting teleportation point, and the second 'T' is the destination teleportation point.\n  \n  Output:\n  - A single integer representing the minimum number of moves required to reach the target point. If it is impossible to reach the target, output '-1'.\n  \n  Example 1:\n  Input:\n  5 5\n  1 1\n  5 5\n  .....\n  .###.\n  .###.\n  .###.\n  .....\n  Output:\n  8\n  \n  Example 2:\n  Input:\n  5 5\n  1 1\n  5 5\n  .....\n  .###.\n  .###.\n  .T#T.\n  .....\n  Output:\n  6\",\n  \"referenceSolution\": \"function optimalRobotPath(grid: string[], startX: number, startY: number, targetX: number, targetY: number): number {\\n    const n = grid.length;\\n    const m = grid[0].length;\\n    const directions = [[0, 1], [1, 0], [0, -1], [-1, 0]];\\n    const visited = new Array(n).fill(false).map(() => new Array(m).fill(false));\\n    let teleport = null;\\n\\n    for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) {\\n        for (let j = 0; j < m; j++) {\\n            if (grid[i][j] === 'T') {\\n                if (teleport === null) {\\n                    teleport = [i, j];\\n                } else {\\n                    grid[teleport[0]][teleport[1]] = '.';\\n                    grid[i][j] = '.';\\n                }\\n            }\\n        }\\n    }\\n\\n    const queue = [{ x: startX - 1, y: startY - 1, moves: 0 }];\\n    visited[startX - 1][startY - 1] = true;\\n\\n    while (queue.length > 0) {\\n        const { x, y, moves } = queue.shift();\\n\\n        if (x === targetX - 1 && y === targetY - 1) {\\n            return moves;\\n        }\\n\\n        for (const [dx, dy] of directions) {\\n            const newX = x + dx;\\n            const newY = y + dy;\\n\\n            if (newX >= 0 && newX < n && newY >= 0 && newY < m && grid[newX][newY] !== '#' && !visited[newX][newY]) {\\n                visited[newX][newY] = true;\\n                queu...","service":"code-execution-backend api","timestamp":"2026-06-02T16:01:59.329Z"}
