{"level":"error","message":"AI returned invalid JSON in generateProblem","raw":"{\n  \"title\": \"Optimal Playlist Scheduler\",\n  \"slug\": \"optimal-playlist-scheduler\",\n  \"description\": \"You are a music streaming service developer tasked with creating an optimal playlist scheduler. Given a list of songs with their durations and a target playlist duration, your goal is to select a subset of songs such that the total duration is as close as possible to the target duration without exceeding it. If multiple subsets have the same total duration, return the subset with the maximum number of songs. If there are still ties, return any valid subset.\n\nInput:\n- A string representing a list of integers, where each integer is the duration of a song. The list is comma-separated.\n- A string representing the target playlist duration as an integer.\n\nOutput:\n- A string representing a list of integers, where each integer is the index of the selected song in the original list. The list is comma-separated.\n\nConstraints:\n- 1 <= number of songs <= 50\n- 1 <= duration of each song <= 1000\n- 1 <= target playlist duration <= 5000\n\nExamples:\nExample 1:\nInput: \"10,20,30,40\", \"60\"\nOutput: \"0,1,2\"\n\nExample 2:\nInput: \"100,200,300,400\", \"800\"\nOutput: \"0,1,2\"\n\",\n  \"referenceSolution\": \"function optimalPlaylistScheduler(songs: string, target: string): string {\\n  const durations = songs.split(',').map(Number);\\n  const targetDuration = Number(target);\\n  const n = durations.length;\\n  const dp = Array.from({ length: n + 1 }, () => Array(targetDuration + 1).fill(-1));\\n  const selectedSongs = Array.from({ length: n + 1 }, () => Array(targetDuration + 1).fill([]));\\n\\n  function knapsack(index: number, currentDuration: number): number {\\n    if (index === 0) return 0;\\n    if (dp[index][currentDuration] !== -1) return dp[index][currentDuration];\\n\\n    let exclude = knapsack(index - 1, currentDuration);\\n    let include = 0;\\n    if (durations[index - 1] <= currentDuration) {\\n      include = durations[index - 1] + knapsack(index - 1, currentDuration - durations[index - 1]);\\n    }\\n\\n    if (include > exclude) {\\n      dp[index][currentDuration] = include;\\n      selectedSongs[index][currentDuration] = [...selectedSongs[index - 1][currentDuration - durations[index - 1]], index - 1];\\n    } else {\\n      dp[index][currentDuration] = exclude;\\n      selectedSongs[index][currentDuration] = selectedSongs[index - 1][currentDuration];\\n    }\\n\\n    return dp[index][currentDuration];\\n  }\\n\\n  knapsack(n, targetDuration);\\n  const result = selectedSongs[n][targetDuration];\\n  return result.join(',');\\n}\",\n  \"testCases\": [\n    {\"input\": \"10,20,30,40\", \"expected\": \"0,1,2\", \"isHidden\": false},\n    {\"input\": \"100,200,300,400\", \"expected\": \"0,1,2\", \"isHidden\": false},\n    {\"input\": \"5,10,15,20,25\", \"expected\": \"0,1,2,3\", \"isHidden\": true},\n    {\"input\": \"1,2,3,4,5,6,7,8,9\", \"expected\": \"0,1,2,3,4,5,6\", \"isHidden\": true},\n    {\"input\": \"10,20,30,40,50\", \"expected\": \"0,1,2,3\", \"isHidden\": true},\n    {\"input\": \"50,100,150,200,250\", \"expected\": \"0,1,2\", \"isHidden\": true},\n    {\"inp...","service":"code-execution-backend api","timestamp":"2026-06-04T07:50:36.500Z"}
